[Music]  every year forbes scours the globe  looking for every billionaire on the  planet and this year even amid the war  in ukraine chinese tech crackdown and  markets that are struggling kind of all  around the globe we still found 2  68 billionaires they're worth a  collective 12.7 trillion dollars that's  with a t  uh which is an incredible amount of  money but actually 400 billion dollars  less than they were worth last year and  there are 87 fewer billionaires in the  world than last year there are a lot of  billionaires behind decacorn companies  which are companies that are valued at  at least 10 billion dollars it used to  be that if you were a  venture funded company and you hit a  billion dollars in valuation you were  called a unicorn and it was extremely  impressive and these days a billion  dollars is uh you know kind of not  enough the really impressive metric is  decacorns companies that are worth at  least 10 billion and we found something  like 30 uh decacorns and there are  billionaires behind a lot of those  another major trend with billionaires  this year is that oil and gas and energy  billionaires are doing extremely well i  mean you'd see high prices at the pump  the billionaires behind oil and gas are  just really thriving these days  global supply chain issues have made it  difficult to get all sorts of goods like  we all know and a lot of companies have  warned their investors that their bottom  lines might be impacted by these supply  chain issues but there's always someone  somewhere profiting no matter what's  going on in the world  and in this case it's shipping and  logistics companies who are really  having banner years and record profits  and that's adding billions of dollars to  the fortunes of the billionaires behind  those companies people like klaus  michael cuna and gm luigi and rafaela  aponte so despite everything that's  going on in the world  more than a thousand billionaires are  richer than they were a year ago  and no one got richer over the past year  than elon musk who tops the billionaires  list for the first time ever musk is  worth 219 billion dollars this year  which is 68 billion dollars more than he  was worth a year ago thanks to soaring  tesla stock  behind elon musk is jeff bezos who is  the second richest person in the world  with 171 billion dollars to his name  after bezos is bernard arneau who's  worth 158 billion then bill gates at  number four with 129 billion and warren  buffett is the fifth richest person in  the world this year worth 118 billion  dollars well there are a lot of  billionaires who are doing really well  there are some that are not doing so  well and you know one group of  billionaires that are in general not  doing very well would be russian  billionaires  so an oligarch generally refers to  people who are very wealthy business  people  who have some kind of political or  social influence when it comes to  to russia specifically  we often look at sort of two time  periods in which oligarchs  arose  one is the original oligarchs who made  their fortunes in the 1990s  during the very chaotic privatization  area after the collapse of the soviet  union  when a lot of state assets were  sold to  private investors on the cheap  especially through a now infamous  voucher system under president boris  yeltsin  and then there was sort of another wave  of oligarchs that arose after uh  vladimir putin rose to power in 2000 a  lot of the people in that group tended  to be  individuals who had close ties to putin  from the early 90s or even before then  and who were able to enrich themselves  thanks to their close ties to putin  generally right oligarch is people who  still have political influence but that  can also sort of refer to how they made  their fortune you know some some  original oligarchs from the 1990s then  fell out of favor actually when putin  was in power  but they were still oligarchs  [Music]  the war in ukraine has had a pretty  significant impact on the wealth of  oligarchs that we track it forms we  estimate that there's around 89  oligarchs in russia several of whom have  actually been sanctioned recently by our  estimates these oligarchs were worth a  collective 290 billion dollars on march  11 which is the date that we finalized  the valuations for our 2022 world  billionaires list and we estimate that  they've lost around 240 billion dollars  so nearly half of their pre-war network  since january before the war began so  the richest person in russia and also  the richest person we consider an  oligarch in russia is vladimir lisin and  we currently estimate his net worth  about 18.4 billion dollars  for context he was worth around 31  billion before the war began in january  better release lisa rose to to fame sort  of in in the 1990s when he was cutting  his teeth in the brutal aluminum wars  today lee sin draws his fortune from  the nlmk group which is a very large  manufacturer of steel products  so since the war began  several assets owned by  sanctioned russian millionaires and  oligarchs have been frozen that means  that these assets can no longer be used  by these individuals and they can't get  any economic benefit from them such as  selling them or renting them but they  still legally own them they have not  been seized by governments  in any of these countries  so we estimate that more than 23 billion  dollars in assets have been hit by  western sanctions since the beginning of  the war perhaps the most prominent  example is roman abramovich's english  premier league soccer team chelsea fc  which is being sold now and the british  government has said that none of the  proceeds will go to abramovic then  another great example is alisher usmanov  who has been sanctioned by the eu and  the uk and the u.s he owns an airbus  a340 300 jet which is blocked by the us  he also has a yacht that is made by  sanctions in germany it's the largest  yacht in the world and is among the at  least 1.5 billion dollars in yachts that  have been hit by western sanctions  he also owns several homes in the uk  which have been blocked by the british  government meaning that he cannot rent  them or sell them or because there's a  travel ban in place against him in the  uk he can't travel there either his  homes in the uk are part of the at least  2.4 billion dollars in real estate that  has been sanctioned so far by western  authorities it's very difficult even for  governments to  actually ascertain who owns these assets  several of these oligarchs simply  transferred ownership of their assets  such as real estate  to relatives or folks associates so as  long as these individuals are able to  get around the sanctions by  selling  certain stakes or transferring ownership  it's still difficult to see if this will  actually have an impact on them long  term of course they can no longer travel  to much of the west and it will be very  difficult for them to  invest in any asset in the west it's  still an open question whether it will  actually have an impact on their network

